      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is impossible to know if change is possible while you are trapped in this heavy rhythm, but history shows that pain often follows a wave pattern where temporary lulls provide the strength to break the cycle differently. People do not just get used to the weight forever; instead, those who survive eventually find new perspectives or support that shifts how the burden feels, even if the numbers remain the same right now. Please consider telling a therapist specifically about this feeling of hopelessness, as hearing a stranger say \"you don't have to carry this alone\" can sometimes be the first crack in the loop where light gets in.",
      "source": "target",
